schema_spec:
Key parts of minimal-jsoncall-schema:
- type: string | number | boolean | object | array | enum | union
- properties: { name: { type: 'string', required: true, example: 'alice' } }
- union: [ {discriminator: 'kind', mapping: { 'file': {properties: {...}}, 'url': {...} } } ]
- coerce: true|false (only allowed on top-level primitive fields)
- deprecated_aliases: ['oldName1', 'old_name'] -> auto-mapped with warning
Example (literal string - for illustration): {
  "type":"object",
  "properties":{
    "user":{"type":"string","required":true,"coerce":true},
    "payload":{"union":[{"discriminator":"type","mapping":{"text":{"properties":{"text":{"type":"string"}}},"file":{"properties":{"b64":{"type":"string"}}}}}] }
}
Notes: Keep keywords minimal so SDKs can implement fast validators, and ensure schema documents remain human-readable and compact.
